22:["$","$L39",null,{"faqs":[{"question":"What is ERP implementation?","answer":"ERP implementation is selecting, configuring, and rolling out an enterprise resource planning system — like NetSuite, SAP, Odoo, or Microsoft Dynamics — then migrating your data and training your team. It puts finance, inventory, operations, and reporting on one connected platform instead of disconnected spreadsheets and tools."},{"question":"What are the phases of an ERP implementation?","answer":"Discovery and planning, vendor selection, solution design, configuration, data migration, integration, testing, training and change management, phased go-live, and post-go-live support. We run them as a fixed-scope, phased method so you see the plan and cost up front and the business never stops during cutover."},{"question":"Why do ERP implementations fail?","answer":"The usual culprits: scope creep, poor-quality migrated data, no change management (the team won't adopt it), over-customization that breaks upgrades, a wrong-fit vendor chosen for the demo, and big-bang go-lives. We de-risk each one with fixed-scope discovery, data cleansing first, built-in change management, configure-over-customize, vendor-by-fit selection, and phased go-live."},{"question":"How much does ERP implementation cost?","answer":"It depends on the number of modules, users, integrations, and data complexity. Senior consulting starts at $50 USD/hour, and we scope a fixed-price discovery first so you get a predictable number before the build. Ongoing support runs hourly or as a fixed monthly retainer."},{"question":"How long does an ERP implementation take?","answer":"A focused single-module rollout can go live in weeks; a full multi-module ERP across a mid-sized business typically runs a few months, in phases. We scope the timeline in discovery so you have a realistic plan before committing."},{"question":"NetSuite, SAP, Odoo, or Dynamics — which ERP should we choose?","answer":"It depends on your size, industry, workflows, and budget — not on who we resell, because we're vendor-neutral. We assess fit across the major platforms and recommend the one (or the mix) that matches how your business actually runs. The right ERP is rarely the most expensive or most complex one."},{"question":"What is AI ERP, and can we add AI to our existing ERP?","answer":"AI ERP (or agentic ERP) is where business systems are heading: instead of only storing data, the ERP acts on it through AI agents. You don't have to replace your current system to benefit. If you already run an ERP, we connect AI agents under your company's umbrella — across all your available data — to speed up analysis, quotations, and process automation today."}],"id":"faq","title":"What teams ask before an ERP project.","fill":true}]
